# ============================================================================
#  .gitignore — keep the repo small; don't commit regenerable build output.
#
#  NOTE: the vendored GDCM binaries in the repo root (gdcmconv.exe, gdcm*.dll,
#  msvcp120.dll, msvcr120.dll, socketxx.dll) are build INPUTS referenced by
#  package.json > build.win.extraResources. They are intentionally NOT ignored
#  so a fresh clone can still build the Windows installer.
#
#  They are the 32-bit (x86) GDCM 3.2.7 build, deliberately: the installer is
#  ia32 and the sender is GOARCH=386, so x86 is the one architecture that runs
#  on 32-bit Windows AND on 64-bit Windows (via WOW64). The superseded x64 set
#  is kept under third_party/gdcm-x64/ for reference only — nothing ships it.
# ============================================================================

# ── Node / Electron ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# electron-builder / packaged output (installers, dmg, zip, unpacked apps)
dist/
out/
release/
# NB: do NOT ignore build/ — electron-builder uses it for icon.icns/entitlements.

# ── Go build output (regenerated by build.bat / build.ps1 / build-mac.sh) ────
# The sender binaries are compiled artifacts, not sources.
/tarang-sender.exe
/tarang-sender
/tarang-sender-arm64
/tarang-sender-amd64
/tarang-sender-darwin-arm64
/tarang-sender-darwin-amd64
mac-build/

# Go test / coverage / profiling
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
*.prof

# ── Logs & runtime data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
*.db
*.tmp

# ── OS cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db

# ── Editor / tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.claude/settings.local.json
